-- World scaling (core WorldScale.h): ContentTuning rows for levels N to 60, N = 1..59 (IDs 8100000 + N), sent to the client
-- as hotfixes (ContentTuning, table hash 3174446591; hotfix_data 81000959-81001017). A vanilla creature of level N that may
-- scale is given row 8100000 + N; the client then shows each player the creature at their own level within the range
-- (tested in game: Corwin Oakheart on row 8100001 showed level 5 / 138 health to a level 5 and 1 / 57 to a level 1).
-- The client's own ContentTuning.db2 has only 100 rows, none for the open world. Apply to the `hotfixes` database;
-- restart worldserver.
DELETE FROM content_tuning WHERE ID BETWEEN 8100001 AND 8100059;
DELETE FROM hotfix_data WHERE Id BETWEEN 81000959 AND 81001017;

